# CODEOWNERS — jolarca-control
#
# READ THIS BEFORE CITING THIS FILE AS A CONTROL (docs/drift-findings.md D-20).
#
# The approving-review count is 0 fleet-wide (solo-era deviation, D-04), so it
# is tempting to call CODEOWNERS "the human gate". It is not, and it cannot be:
#
#   1. jolarca-dev has exactly one member. That member is the author of every
#      PR, and GitHub does not let you approve your own pull request. So there
#      is nobody who can supply a code-owner approval.
#   2. Verified empirically elsewhere in this fleet: jolarca-infrastructure
#      PR #26 merged with require_code_owner_reviews = true, ZERO reviews, and
#      an empty requested_reviewers list. The same is true of every sampled
#      merged PR in the org. GitHub does not block the merge.
#
# So this file ROUTES review and documents intended ownership. It does not
# ENFORCE anything today. The gates that actually decide are automated:
# required status checks, the apply.yml plan-refusal gate, prevent_destroy, and
# the STATE_MIGRATION_COMPLETE hard gate. Do not represent this file to an
# auditor as human segregation of duties.
#
# Unlike the other five repositories, the entries below at least name a real
# principal in THIS org (@JourneyOfLife). The rest of the fleet names
# @journeyoflife-org/* teams and a nonexistent @jol-infrastructure org — a live
# breach of ADR-0004 R4, tracked as D-20 and RA-07. Fixing those is required
# regardless of what happens here.
#
# When teams are created (second-operator onboarding, D-10), replace the
# individual with the team slug in the SAME PR that raises D-04 to 1 — do not do
# one without the other, or you will have an approval count nobody can satisfy.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS routes review; it cannot require N approvers. The count is
# enforced by branch protection (branch-protection.tf), not by this file.

# Default: the organization owner
*                       @JourneyOfLife

# Control plane core — a change here can alter every repo in the org
/repos/                 @JourneyOfLife
/policy/                @JourneyOfLife
/*.tf                   @JourneyOfLife
/terraform.tfvars       @JourneyOfLife

# CI itself — an unprotected pipeline is an unenforced policy
/.github/workflows/     @JourneyOfLife
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @JourneyOfLife
/scripts/               @JourneyOfLife

# Compliance evidence and doctrine
/docs/                  @JourneyOfLife
/audit/                 @JourneyOfLife

# The findings register and the migration gate: changes here change what the
# organization believes to be true about itself.
/docs/drift-findings.md         @JourneyOfLife
/docs/state-migration-runbook.md @JourneyOfLife
/docs/threat-model.md           @JourneyOfLife
